; The ONE variable: whether a ParallaxBackground hosts the canvas its Control
; children draw on. `ParallaxBackground` derives from `CanvasLayer`
; (parallax_background.h:34) and defaults its `layer` to -100, so the red rect
; below belongs to a canvas UNDER the world's and the blue world polygon covers
; it. A Control walk that hoists past the ParallaxBackground puts the red rect
; on the world canvas instead, where its canvas-root rank is after the polygon
; and it covers the polygon instead. The two rects overlap for exactly that
; reason; unit-parallax-background.tscn carries no Control at all, so it cannot
; see this.

